docs:
Installed `GooeyToaster` and `gooeyToast` (`@/components/ui/gooey-toast`), an add-on over shadcn's `sonner` item.

Render the toaster once, near the root:

```tsx
import { GooeyToaster } from "@/components/ui/gooey-toast";

<GooeyToaster position="bottom-right" />
```

Then call it anywhere:

```tsx
import { gooeyToast } from "@/components/ui/gooey-toast";

gooeyToast.success("Saved");
gooeyToast.error("Connection lost", { description: "Check your network and try again." });
gooeyToast.promise(save(), { loading: "Saving...", success: "Saved", error: "Failed" });
```

It renders its own Sonner `<Toaster>`, so use it instead of shadcn's `<Toaster />`, not next to it. The stylesheet is injected by the toaster; no CSS import is needed. Theme it with the toaster's `theme` (`light` or `dark`) and per toast with `fillColor`, `borderColor` and `classNames`.

Ported from goey-toast by anl331 (MIT); the license notice is at the end of every file.

